Zen's generated trigram prediction table is derived from the public English
NUS SMS Corpus maintained by the Web, Information Retrieval and Natural
Language Processing Group at the National University of Singapore.

Source: https://github.com/kite1988/nus-sms-corpus
Archive SHA-256: bf73d77fce35c703dab21826cd2c1698205358c2c25b2d43da1f08671b825bdc

Citation:
Tao Chen and Min-Yen Kan (2013). Creating a Live, Public Short Message Service
Corpus: The NUS SMS Corpus. Language Resources and Evaluation, 47(2), 299-355.

The original messages are not redistributed by this repository. The generated
table contains only 300 ranked, dictionary-filtered phrase identifiers. Zen's
child-safe dictionary filter excludes words outside the firmware vocabulary.
